  "worked_solution": "Previously, we found that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}=-10x{y}^{2}-4x,\\,\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}=-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y.\n$$\n\nComputing the second partial derivatives, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(-10x{y}^{2}-4x)=-10{y}^{2}-4 \\\\ \\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202x\u2202y} & =\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202y\u2202x}=\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(-10x{y}^{2}-4x)=-20xy \\\\ \\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y)=-12{y}^{2}-10{x}^{2}+20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
